						<tr>
							<td height="50" colspan="3" valign="top" class="windowbg2" align="left"><div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1606.msg17629#msg17629">Quote from: Kinladar on June 27, 2005, 07:40:20 am</a></div><div class="quote"><div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1606.msg17628#msg17628">Quote from: simplee on June 27, 2005, 05:55:56 am</a></div><div class="quote">1) All games have a dwindling subscriber base.  WoW included.   I don&#039;t see WoW being as successful as EQ was for as long as it was.<br /></div><br />But, games like WoW, still have not reached thier pinnacle yet in total subscriber base. However, the only downside to WoW, is if you are not really into PvP, there&#039;s not a great deal to do at 60. Some cool stuff on the horizon, but what will keep WoW sucessfull in the long run is, they have released a great deal of content, that SoE would have held back for a paid for expansion, for free. </div><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote"></div><br />I don&#039;t think its right to say that WoW hasn&#039;t reached it&#039;s pinnacle yet.&nbsp; There&#039;s no way to tell.&nbsp; With people already leaving the game, and with Vanguard on the horizon, WoW might have already hit it&#039;s peak.&nbsp; Then again, maybe not.&nbsp; There&#039;s just no way to tell.<br /><br /><div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1606.msg17629#msg17629">Quote from: Kinladar on June 27, 2005, 07:40:20 am</a></div><div class="quote"><div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1606.msg17628#msg17628">Quote from: simplee on June 27, 2005, 05:55:56 am</a></div><div class="quote">2) If OoW and DoN were small steps in the right direction, what makes you think they can&#039;t continue to make progress little by little?  I actually liked the progression set up by PoP and GoD, thout admittedly I didn&#039;t at first.  There&#039;s a certain feeling of accomplishment by making it to each next level.  I can&#039;t say that about OoW or DoN, though I enjoy those expansions too.<br /></div><br />The major reason why OoW, and DoN are small steps, is because PoP, and GoD were gigantic steps in the wrong direction for the health of the game. Now I found PoP to be pretty fun the first couple times through all the events, but the continual reflagging, and other BS needed to keep a raiding guild going killed me. The lack of things for many casual players to do, killed them. GoD took that to the next power, granted many of the trials to get like Kod Taz flagged were single group, but to really have any chance of getting through them, you wanted Plane of Time Geared players, at least until it was discovered that a Druid/Chanter combo could duo the hardest of them, in Tipt and Vxed complete. </div><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote"></div><br />The backflagging process has changed drastically now.&nbsp; There&#039;s no need to go back and hit mobs repeatedly, and even with GoD, there are backflag quests, that require maybe a group to complete, and can be done in a day (ok, one raid mob too). <br /><br /><div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1606.msg17629#msg17629">Quote from: Kinladar on June 27, 2005, 07:40:20 am</a></div><div class="quote"><div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=1606.msg17628#msg17628">Quote from: simplee on June 27, 2005, 05:55:56 am</a></div><div class="quote">3) There&#039;s no &quot;fix&quot; to the classes.  I don&#039;t see it as being possible.  Changing something within one class, angers another.  And you can&#039;t simply just consolidate classes...people picked a class and leveled it up, changing it at that point would do nothing but piss people off further.  Even berserkers.<br /></div><br />There is, just that they don&#039;t have the guts to take the real steps nessesary to make it happen. They really need to trim down the number of classes.<br /><br />I honestly think the Devs think they are doing a good job, but they are delusional. I&#039;m generally a realist, but in this case, I really think the higher ups are trying to kill this game off. I hate making random theories, but it&#039;s evident with how little they are doing to really make this game publicly acceptable, that they don&#039;t want it to bounce back.</div> <div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote"></div><br />You can&#039;t trim down the number of classes without pissing off half the player base.&nbsp; How would you feel if they suddenly decided to &quot;merge&quot; the ranger class with another?&nbsp; All the work you put into Kinlader, all pulled out from under you?&nbsp; Should they keep characters at the level they&#039;re at, or just simply start deleting characters of a certain class?<br /><br />If they were trying to kill the game off, they&#039;d simply stop making expansions.&nbsp; Seeing as another one is due out in September, I don&#039;t think thats the case.</td>
